# Index artifacts.
#
# NOT committed. At 250 source rows they were 22MB combined and shipping them
# inside the repository was the right call. At 10,000 rows they are 336MB
# (FAISS) + 445MB (metadata), and GitHub hard-rejects any file over 100MB, so
# that is no longer an option regardless of preference.
#
# They are published as GitHub Release assets instead: 2GB per file is allowed
# there, the bytes do not count against repository size, and public-repo
# downloads are not bandwidth-metered the way Git LFS is. setup.ps1 and
# setup.sh fetch them automatically, so a fresh clone is still runnable
# without a 5.4-hour rebuild.
#
# Benchmark and comparison results stay ignored too: they are regenerated per
# machine and would only create noisy diffs.
artifacts/*
backend/artifacts/*

# --- Logs ---
*.log
logs/

